usage: auto.py [-h] [-f CONFIG.yaml] [--domain DOMAIN_TYPE] [--scope SCOPE]
               [--provider PROVIDER_NAME] [--model MODEL]
               [--retries MAX_RETRIES] [--temp TEMPERATURE] [--stream]
               [--thinking] [--no-scaffold] [--no-diagram] [--context PATH]
               [--name NAME] [--desc-file PATH] [--entry NAMES]
               [--zoom-to TARGET] [--zoom-levels ZOOM_LEVELS] [--churn]
               [--windings N] [--max-ob3ects N] [--concurrency N]
               [description ...]

Auto-design an Ob3ect from a description.

positional arguments:
  description           Natural-language description (omit when using -f)

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  -f CONFIG.yaml, --yaml CONFIG.yaml, --file CONFIG.yaml
                        Batch-imscribe every entity listed in a YAML (this
                        pipeline's own batch loop)
  --domain DOMAIN_TYPE  Domain type hint (biological, computational,
                        alchemical, ...)
  --scope SCOPE         Scope: local | mesoscale | maximal (default: local)
  --provider PROVIDER_NAME
                        Override provider (openrouter, deepseek, local)
  --model MODEL         Model ID passed to the provider (e.g. deepseek-chat,
                        qwen3-235b-a22b)
  --retries MAX_RETRIES
                        Max design retries per entity; 'inf'/'infinite' =
                        retry until success (default: inf)
  --temp TEMPERATURE
  --stream              Stream the design call's output as it generates.
                        Tokens go to stderr so stdout still carries only the
                        artifact; the full text is returned either way, so
                        nothing downstream changes.
  --thinking            Enable <thinking> tokens in local Qwen model (default:
                        off)
  --no-scaffold         Suppress Lean scaffold output
  --no-diagram          Suppress symbolic wiring diagram output
  --context PATH        File or directory of domain documents to include as
                        context (.md/.txt/.lean/.py/.tex/.json; up to 500 KB
                        total)
  --name NAME           Name the imscription explicitly. Without this the name
                        is derived from the description, which forces a
                        description carrying LaTeX or punctuation to double as
                        an identifier
  --desc-file PATH      Read the description from a file instead of the
                        command line. A shell eats $A, backticks and braces
                        before the pipeline sees them, so a statement in LaTeX
                        arrives silently altered
  --entry NAMES         Comma-separated catalog entry names to inject as
                        context (e.g. --entry yhwh,dark_matter,proton)
  --zoom-to TARGET      Design a zoom chain from DESCRIPTION (∈=0, finest) to
                        TARGET (∈=N-1, coarsest)
  --zoom-levels ZOOM_LEVELS
                        Number of levels in the zoom chain (default: 4)
  --churn               Wind the pipeline back over its own output: imscribe
                        the description, fold the resulting ob3ect into the
                        context it came from, then imscribe each of its steps
                        in turn
  --windings N          How many full turns to churn (default: 2). One winding
                        is the root alone; each further winding imscribes
                        every step of every ob3ect from the turn before
  --max-ob3ects N       Stop the churn after this many ob3ects (default: 200)
  --concurrency N       How many sibling ob3ects to imscribe at once during a
                        churn (default: 4). A local server has a fixed number
                        of slots; queueing past them only moves the wait.
